FFF webmap — verification suite
===============================

These are the probes that caught every regression so far. They drive the REAL page in headless
Chromium (Playwright) against a local static server, so they assert on what a browser actually does
(request log, pixels, DOM), not on what the source looks like.

Setup (once)
------------
    cd Webmap
    npm i --no-save --no-package-lock playwright     # installs into ./node_modules (gitignored)
    npx playwright install chromium                  # downloads the matching browser (~150 MB, once)

Serve the site (HTTP is required — boundaries and grantees are fetch()-ed, file:// shows nothing):

    python3 -m http.server 6115 --directory .        # from Webmap/ → http://localhost:6115

Run
---
    cd Webmap
    node tests/verify_web_ui.js          # console/page errors, map container, tiles
    node tests/probe_geocsv_source.js    # the geocsv is the ONLY grantee source (see below)
    node tests/probe_women_mode.js       # Women-Led mode shows exactly the 13 geocoded women-led orgs
    node tests/probe_mode_exclusive.js   # overview / evolution / women modes are mutually exclusive
    node tests/probe_scope_full.js       # polygon-click aggregates: PIP precedence, national totals
    node tests/probe_sankey_pip.js       # sankey province/palika come from PIP (no bare state codes, wards merged)
    node tests/probe_sankey_interactive.js # the 6 column dropdowns: redraw on change, totals preserved
    node tests/probe_layout_split.js      # map/panel split: legend hidden, 50% default, drag resize, Nepal refit
    node tests/probe_investment_mode.js  # Investment map tab: panel hidden elsewhere, expands in-mode
    node tests/probe_sankey_table.js    # the chains as a table under the charts (totals == chart roots)
    node tests/probe_sankey_fit.js      # the charts FIT the strip: no clipping at 5 panel heights + real drags
    node tests/probe_org_names.js      # display-name tidy: redundant brackets dropped, acronyms kept
    node tests/probe_hover_unlink.js     # marker/cluster hover must NOT write the bottom panel
    node tests/probe_legend_pie.js       # legend placement + LoA/DBG pie & bar colours
    node tests/probe_evo_amount.js       # evolution grant-amount column adds up to the national total
    node tests/probe_evo_fit.js          # the evolution table fits inside the 340px panel
    node tests/measure_load.js           # NOT a pass/fail probe: prints page weight + startup timing

Boundary rebuilds
-----------------
    python3 tests/boundary_pip_check.py data/District.geojson      # baseline, exit 0
    python3 tests/boundary_pip_check.py /tmp/District.min.geojson  # candidate, exit 1 on a moved border

What "green" looks like: every probe prints `PASS …` lines and ends with `ALL PASS` (or no `FAIL` line),
and exits non-zero on failure, so `for f in tests/probe_*.js; do node $f || echo "FAILED $f"; done` is a
usable one-liner. Expected counts live inside the probes (36 orgs, 13 women-led, 2,288,256 USD, 77/7/1/1/33
boundary paths) — update them deliberately when the data changes, never to make a red probe green.
